CPC4MEGA65 / CoreCPC:
---------------------

  CPC4MEGA65 is an Amstrad CPC 6128 core for the MEGA65, ported on top of
  the MiSTer2MEGA65 framework and built on the MiSTer-devel Amstrad_MiSTer
  core. The MEGA65 port itself (this repository), including the
  MiSTer2MEGA65 integration, the real 3.5" floppy drive subsystem (MFM
  data separator, track formatter, disk copier and write-back) and all
  MEGA65-specific work, was done by Jose Daniel Fernandez Santos
  (dfsantos), with the assistance of Claude Code (Anthropic) as an AI
  pair-programming tool throughout the design, debugging and
  documentation work.

  CPC4MEGA65 is a port of MiSTer-devel's Amstrad_MiSTer
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Amstrad_MiSTer
      Our fork, with every change documented in doc/m2m/exceptions.md:
      https://github.com/dfernande132/Amstrad_MiSTer (branch cpc4mega65)

  Significant contributors to the MiSTer Amstrad core and the components
  it is built from:

  * Sorgelig - the MiSTer Amstrad core, UM6845R CRTC, Amstrad MMU, and the
    MiSTer packaging of the T80 CPU and YM2149

  * Gyorgy Szombathelyi (gyurco) - the uPD765 floppy disk controller
    (u765) and the GA40010 gate array implementation

  * Gerald - "40010-simplified_V03.pdf", the gate array documentation the
    GA40010 implementation is based on

  * Daniel Wallner and TobiFlex - the T80 Z80-compatible CPU core

  * MikeJ - the YM2149 sound chip core

  The Amstrad CPC hardware itself was designed by Amstrad plc; the CPC
  firmware and Locomotive BASIC are the work of Locomotive Software. This
  project reimplements the hardware only and ships no Amstrad ROMs.

Other than that and my own work, CoreCPC uses:
----------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and on-screen-menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/
